  stem:"A male newborn born at 37 weeks of gestation is examined at 24 hours of age because of yellow skin down to the chest. He is active and feeding well. Mother and infant are both blood group O, Rh-positive, and the direct antiglobulin test is negative. Total serum bilirubin is 12 mg/dL with direct bilirubin 0.5 mg/dL. Using the AAP 2022 thresholds, what is the most appropriate management?",
